# PRIVATE KEYS. Never commit.
#
# src/demo.js writes generated keypairs here so reruns reuse the same devnet
# accounts. They are devnet keys and worth nothing — but the same file layout is
# what a mainnet deployment would produce, and the habit of having .keys/ tracked
# is the one that eventually costs somebody their treasury.
#
# git also keeps deleted content forever. A key committed once and removed in the
# next commit is still in the history, still fetchable, and must be treated as
# compromised from that moment on. So this line goes in before `git init`, not
# after the first mistake.
.keys/
*.key
*.pem
id.json
keypair.json

node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
